# LinuxShot desktop entry. Two things in this file are identity, not cosmetics,
# and getting either wrong breaks the GNOME screen-capture permission.
#
# 1. The file name. The portal derives our app id from the systemd user unit we
#    run in, and launching through this entry puts us in
#    app-gnome-io.github.minnyat.linuxshot-<pid>.scope - so the app id follows
#    THIS FILE'S NAME. It must stay io.github.minnyat.linuxshot.desktop in every
#    channel (AppImage, .deb, .rpm, Flatpak, tarball, autostart), matching
#    singleInstanceID in main.go. A channel that ships the same content as
#    linuxshot.desktop yields app id "linuxshot" instead: a second permission
#    prompt, a second stored permission, and revoking one leaves the other.
#    Worse, if BOTH entries are ever installed, gnome-shell 46 resolves the
#    StartupWMClass "linuxshot" to the entry whose own id matches it
#    (startup_wm_class_is_exact_match in shell-app-system.c), i.e. to
#    linuxshot.desktop - so an instance launched from the correct entry has
#    portal id io.github.minnyat.linuxshot while the shell calls the focused
#    window linuxshot, and the request is refused outright. Never ship a second
#    entry carrying StartupWMClass=linuxshot.
#
# 2. StartupWMClass=linuxshot - exact, lowercase. Measured on gnome-shell 46.0:
#    our window carries WM_CLASS = "linuxshot", "Linuxshot" (from
#    g_set_prgname("linuxshot"), which Wails sets from the Linux ProgramName
#    option in main.go) and no _GTK_APPLICATION_ID. The shell looks the window's
#    WM_CLASS up in a plain string-keyed table of StartupWMClass values, so the
#    match is case-sensitive and it is the lowercase instance part that matches.
#    Without it the shell cannot map our window to this entry, so it does not
#    consider us the focused app and xdg-desktop-portal refuses the request.
#
# StartupNotify is false on purpose: with minimize-to-tray enabled main.go
# starts with no window mapped, and a startup-notification sequence that nothing
# completes leaves the shell showing a launch spinner until it times out.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=LinuxShot
GenericName=Screenshot Tool
Comment=Capture your screen, annotate it, and share the result
Exec=linuxshot
Icon=io.github.minnyat.linuxshot
Terminal=false
Categories=Graphics;2DGraphics;RasterGraphics;
Keywords=screenshot;screen;capture;snip;snapshot;annotate;region;print screen;
StartupNotify=false
StartupWMClass=linuxshot
